: "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked, but as two separate bookings instead of one combined booking.\n\n**Booked (both confirmed):**\n- **Flight R0001:** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. A $199 flight was available but has one stop.\n- **Hotel R0002:** Midtown Lodge, $189/night, 2 nights from 2026-11-12, $378. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total: $667.** That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What happened:** I tried to book both together with `book_trip`, but the request timed out. When I retried it, the system said the flight had gone through but the hotel step had failed. Dana's reservation list confirmed only the flight was booked. I then booked the hotel on its own. Her reservations now show exactly one flight and one hotel, with no duplicate charges.", "type": "text"}]}]}